# Vercel builds the Next.js app from this directory. The FastAPI backend now
# lives at ../backend, outside this tree entirely, because Vercel treats any
# main.py plus requirements.txt beneath its root directory as a second
# application to deploy - and offered to mount it at /api/backend, which is
# where src/app/api/backend/[...path]/route.ts already lives. That route is the
# proxy that reads the caller session from cookies and attaches it as a bearer
# token, so losing the path to a FastAPI deployment would send every backend
# call out unauthenticated.
#
# Database migrations are applied through the Supabase SQL editor, not by the
# web build.
supabase/
